{"result":"{
  "id": "18943",
  "key": "SFCC-562",
  "description": "As a Site Admin, I want canonical tags output on all indexable pages, referencing the preferred URL for that storefront, so that duplicate content is avoided and link equity is correctly attributed to the canonical URL.\n\nCovers both DMU-022 (canonical on all indexable pages) and DMU-023 (canonical on filtered/faceted PLP URLs pointing to the base PLP) - merged into one story since they're a single implementation surface with a shared codepath (one function, one extra branch for the filtered case). Zimmermann also want the ability to override the canonical target on specific indexable filter pages via Business Manager - scoped into this story.\n\nMerged from SFCC-563 on 2026-09-14 (see Confluence page 478248974 footer comment for the rationale). SFCC-563 is retained in Jira as a superseded reference only - do not groom it separately."
}"}

{"result":"{
  "id": "18943",
  "key": "SFCC-562",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "- Every indexable page (homepage, PDP, unfiltered PLP/category, content pages) renders exactly one self-referencing canonical link tag in the page head, using the absolute https URL for the current storefront/locale.\n- No page renders more than one canonical tag.\n- Paginated PLP/category pages (page 2, 3, etc.) each carry their OWN self-referencing canonical - never canonicalized back to page 1 (per Google: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/specialty/ecommerce/pagination-and-incremental-page-loading).\n- Filtered/faceted PLP URLs (colour/size/category filter combinations with no confirmed standalone search value) render a canonical tag pointing to the unfiltered base PLP URL, not a self-reference.\n- Facet combinations Tell No Lies/Sparro confirm as having real standalone search demand (see SFCC-571 dependency) are excluded from that rule and get a self-referencing canonical instead, per SFCC-571's per-facet-type split - never both a robots.txt block and a canonical on the same URL.\n- Business Manager gives a Site Merchandiser a way to override the canonical target on a specific indexable filter URL - exact BM mechanism TBC, see Assumptions.\n- Canonical URL strips tracking/query parameters that aren't part of the page's own identity (e.g. UTM params) - exact allow/deny list TBC, see Assumptions.\n- Canonical tag always reflects the current storefront's own domain/locale prefix - never points cross-storefront.\n- Verified via view-source across at least one page of each template type (home, PDP, category, a paginated category page, and a filtered category page) on each storefront."
  }
}"}

