{"result":"{
  "id": "18954",
  "key": "SFCC-573",
  "summary": "SEO — CollectionPage, BreadcrumbList & ItemList Schema (PLP)",
  "description": "As a Site Admin, I want CollectionPage, BreadcrumbList, and ItemList structured data schema implemented on all PLP pages, so that category pages are eligible for rich results and breadcrumb trails display in search.\n\nBreadcrumbList is the only one of the three with an actual Google Search rich-result feature - CollectionPage and ItemList are valid schema.org markup with no dedicated Google SERP enhancement today, but still useful for AI/GEO crawlers per DMU-043. The Sparro template dependency is narrowed to a couple of modelling preferences, not the base shape - see Technical Notes and Dependencies. Depends on breadcrumb component existing (SFCC-578) for the BreadcrumbList portion only - ItemList/CollectionPage don't share that blocker.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "DMU-039",
    "Squad-B"
  ]
}"}

{"result":"{
  "id": "18954",
  "key": "SFCC-573",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "- BreadcrumbList: itemListElement array of ListItem{position (1-indexed), name, item (URL) - item omitted on the final/current-page item per Google's spec}, sourced from whatever breadcrumb path SFCC-578's component computes.\n- ItemList: itemListElement array of ListItem{position, url, name} for each product currently rendered on the PLP page (paginated - only the current page's products, consistent with SFCC-562's per-page-canonical pagination rule) - buildable today from the existing productSearchResult data already available to product-list, independent of the breadcrumb component.\n- CollectionPage: name, description, url (canonical PLP URL per SFCC-562), wrapping the ItemList - confirm with Sparro whether they want this wrapper or a bare ItemList (both valid; Google has no dedicated CollectionPage rich result either way, so this is a modelling preference).\n- Filtered/faceted PLP variants that SFCC-562 canonicalizes to the base PLP do NOT get their own ItemList/CollectionPage describing the filtered subset - the schema always describes the canonical (unfiltered) product set, matching the declared canonical URL."
  }
}"}

