  "summary": "SEO – Indexable Filter Pages with Per-Filter Metadata",
  "description": "As a Site Merchandiser, \n\nI want to flag specific filter combinations (e.g. Dresses + White) as indexable pages with their own clean URL and metadata, \n\nso that Zimmermann can rank for high-value search terms like \"white dresses\" without having to create and maintain a separate category for each one.\n\n----\n\nCurrently, all filtered PLP URLs canonicalise back to the base category page per DMU-023, meaning Google does not index them as standalone pages. This enhancement would allow a merchandiser to opt specific filter combinations into indexability via Business Manager, and set a unique title tag, meta description, and SEO paragraph per combination. The PWA Kit would then render the correct metadata for those URLs.\n\nNote: the SEO agency (Sparro / Tell No Lies) must define the URL structure rules and metadata templates before build can begin. This is a custom build — effort estimate required before prioritisation.",
