  "id": "18140",
  "key": "SFCC-95",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to see contextual page information next to the breadcrumb navigation,\n\n**so that** I can understand where I am on the site and discover relevant content.\n\n----\n\n**Context:**\n\nThis story covers two related UI behaviours tied to the area next to the breadcrumb navigation at the bottom of the page (below Recently Viewed).\n\n**SEO text block:** A set of labelled accordion sections is displayed beneath the Recently Viewed component. The sections are collapsed by default, showing only the section header. Each section can be individually expanded to reveal its SEO copy — for example, category descriptions or editorial content — and collapsed again by clicking the header. The section headings and body copy are CMS-managed in Contentful and are page-contextual; the content rendered depends on the page the shopper is on. This content is independent of the Recently Viewed component itself and is always present on the page regardless of whether Recently Viewed is rendered.\n\n**Conditional background colour:** The Recently Viewed component has its own background colour. When the component is not rendered — for example, when the shopper has no browsing history — the SEO text block would otherwise appear against an orphaned coloured band that doesn't match the white content above it. The background colour of this section must therefore adapt: when Recently Viewed is rendered, it uses the standard component background; when Recently Viewed is not rendered, the background blends with the white section above to avoid a visual break.\n\n\n\nCurrent (needs redesign):\n\n![\"image-20260702-025220.png\"](image-20260702-025220.png)\n\nFigma design reference:\n\n\n![\"image-20260714-032202.png\"](image-20260714-032202.png)",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "# Given a shopper is on a page that has SEO accordion content configured in Contentful, when the page renders, then one or more labelled accordion sections are displayed below the Recently Viewed component, each collapsed by default.\n# Given an accordion section is expanded, when the shopper clicks the section header, then the section collapses to show only the header.\n# Given an accordion section is collapsed, when the shopper clicks the section header, then the section expands to reveal its body content.\n# Given multiple accordion sections are present on the page, when the shopper collapses one section, then other sections remain in their current state.\n# Given the accordion content is managed in Contentful, when a content author updates section headings or body copy, then the changes are reflected on the relevant page without a code deployment.\n# Given a page has no SEO accordion content configured in Contentful, when the page renders, then no accordion section is displayed.\n# Given the Recently Viewed component is not rendered (e.g. the shopper has no browsing history), when the SEO accordion section is present, then its background blends with the white content above to avoid an orphaned coloured band.\n# Given the Recently Viewed component is rendered above the SEO accordion section, when the page renders, then the accordion section displays the standard component background colour."
  }
